30,2,1,talk,May,,"My research shows that the late-evening pilot was a success, but the accessibility programme had mixed results—some lane-priority stretches were just given back to traffic.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"That is concerning. My findings show our late-turn pool is dangerously thin, and roadway crews are well below establishment, though lift maintenance actually has spare capacity.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Interestingly, the mid-city runs are slower than they used to be, but the crowds clear at the same rate. Also, passengers spend more time waiting for connections than at ticket machines.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I found that work in pre-war shells is very risky due to unrecorded voids, and the ferry and rail offices haven't even agreed on passenger data terms.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The financial picture is strained. We have a lapsed grant balance, but our operating and technology budgets were trimmed, and ticketing fees are now higher than our paving budget.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, if the roadway crews are short, we should be very careful about any plan that requires new dedicated lanes or roadworks.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, precisely. Any plan relying on the late-turn pool for overnight work is also a gamble, as overtime is already stretched to the limit.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, if the technology budget is trimmed, can we even afford a major digital overhaul? It seems the passengers are struggling more with connections than with the ticketing process.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, that is a good point. And if we look at the pre-war stations, the hidden voids make any structural work there a potential nightmare for the schedule.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the technology line is indeed tight. We are paying a lot to three different contractors, which seems inefficient, but the capital for new construction is where the lapsed grant sits.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,May,,"It seems we have a conflict between our ambitions and our actual capacity. We have successful pilots for night services, but no people to run them.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, exactly. The ""success"" of a pilot eight years ago doesn't account for the recruitment freeze that has gutted our current rosters.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Midori,,"If the ticketing machines aren't the bottleneck, maybe we should focus on the physical movement of people or the timing of the services.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"But the physical movement in old stations is risky, and the coordination between different operators is currently non-existent.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,We must find a path that doesn't create a long-term financial burden or rely on budgets that have already been trimmed.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,pass,May,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
